Build the dependencies with the parent's exception model

Under Emscripten, cvc5 compiles LibPoly and CaDiCaL with a hard-coded
-fexceptions, because emcc's default -fignore-exceptions would discard
the landing pads their frames need when a cvc5 exception unwinds through
them.  That is right in itself, but it ignores what the rest of the
build uses: a build configured with -fwasm-exceptions ends up with two
incompatible exception models, and the link fails with a few hundred
undefined __resumeException and invoke_* symbols from libpicpolyxx.a and
libcadical.a.  (cvc5's own objects are fine: clang takes the wasm model
when both flags are given.)

So pick the model the parent build is using instead of assuming the
JavaScript one.  A default build, which passes neither flag, is
unaffected -- it still gets -fexceptions.

FindCoCoA.cmake hard-codes -fexceptions the same way; it is left alone
because this build does not pass --cocoa and the change would be
untested here.

Applied by build.sh; see README.md.  Worth sending upstream.

diff --git a/cmake/FindCaDiCaL.cmake b/cmake/FindCaDiCaL.cmake
index 7349252..997d233 100644
--- a/cmake/FindCaDiCaL.cmake
+++ b/cmake/FindCaDiCaL.cmake
@@ -110,8 +110,15 @@ if(NOT CaDiCaL_FOUND_SYSTEM)
   # runs as a CaDiCaL::ExternalPropagator callback, so exceptions it throws
   # from inside the SAT search (e.g. FfTimeoutException) unwind back out
   # through CaDiCaL frames; without this flag their destructors are skipped.
+  # Inherit the parent build's exception model: objects compiled with
+  # -fwasm-exceptions do not link against objects compiled with -fexceptions
+  # (the latter reference __resumeException and friends).
   if(EMSCRIPTEN)
-    string(APPEND CaDiCaL_CXXFLAGS " -fexceptions")
+    if(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS MATCHES "-fwasm-exceptions")
+      string(APPEND CaDiCaL_CXXFLAGS " -fwasm-exceptions")
+    else()
+      string(APPEND CaDiCaL_CXXFLAGS " -fexceptions")
+    endif()
   endif()
 
   # On macOS, we have to set `-isysroot` to make sure that include headers are
diff --git a/cmake/FindPoly.cmake b/cmake/FindPoly.cmake
index df3dd77..b0fe734 100644
--- a/cmake/FindPoly.cmake
+++ b/cmake/FindPoly.cmake
@@ -189,8 +189,15 @@ if(NOT Poly_FOUND_SYSTEM)
   # See FindCaDiCaL.cmake: emcc's default -fignore-exceptions emits no
   # landing pads, so destructors in LibPoly frames an exception unwinds
   # through would be skipped.
+  # Inherit the parent build's exception model: objects compiled with
+  # -fwasm-exceptions do not link against objects compiled with -fexceptions
+  # (the latter reference __resumeException and friends).
   if(EMSCRIPTEN)
-    string(APPEND _poly_cxx_flags " -fexceptions")
+    if(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS MATCHES "-fwasm-exceptions")
+      string(APPEND _poly_cxx_flags " -fwasm-exceptions")
+    else()
+      string(APPEND _poly_cxx_flags " -fexceptions")
+    endif()
   endif()
   if(_poly_cxx_flags)
     string(STRIP "${_poly_cxx_flags}" _poly_cxx_flags)
